Mutation for scripts/joint-official.sh 3/8 (B6-01, A2A-DESIGN §15): anet-official answers without
checking the bearer token its daemon holds, so anything on the host that can open a loopback socket
calls the backend directly — around the daemon's admission, quotas and payment — and can write its own
X-ANet-Caller. Never commit it applied.

Apply in a scratch worktree, never in a checkout anything ships from:

    cd ANet && git apply scripts/mutations/official-no-backend-token.patch
    go build -o "$MUTBIN/anet-official" ./cmd/anet-official   # anet, anet-hub, anet-hub-admin into $MUTBIN as usual
    JOINT_BIN="$MUTBIN" scripts/joint-official.sh

Expected: 3/8 red — the calls without a token or with a wrong one are answered 200 (or 404 for the
unknown path) instead of 401, so the routes can be probed and the backend's log shows fewer than five
refusals. The daemon's own calls still work: it sends the token, which is now not read. The unit-level
twin is TestOnlyTheDaemonGetsIn in cmd/anet-official/server_test.go.

